-- title:
--   Generic Abel–Jacobi reading of a Pl-point of relative Pic⁰
-- statement:
--   The setting is the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring in the $p$-th cyclotomic field.
--
--   *Arithmetic data.* Let $p$ be a prime, $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and $L$ a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, with $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ its fraction field, with $p$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with the tower $A \to L \to K$, and let $j \in K$, nonzero, whose image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ is the coefficient image [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion of the $j$-invariant. Write $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ for [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252), assumed proper, and $X_R$ for the pullback of $X$ along the morphism $\operatorname{Spec} R \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ induced by a given $A$-algebra $R$.
--
--   *Special fibre data.* Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ which is an $A$-algebra, and let $c_1 : C_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$, $c_2 : C_2 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, with closed immersions $i_1, i_2$ of $C_1, C_2$ into $X_k$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$. It is assumed that every point of $X_k$ lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$ (`hcover`), that the fibre product $C_1 \times_{X_k} C_2$ is reduced, and that its cardinality is a natural number $n > 0$.
--
--   *Sections.* Let $\varepsilon$ be a section of $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, and $\varepsilon_1, \varepsilon_2$ sections of $c_1, c_2$, with $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ equal to the base change of $\varepsilon$ to $k$.
--
--   *Relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ data.* Let $D$ be a relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ designation for $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, that is a scheme $D.P$ with a structure morphism $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and a zero section, and assume that $D$ represents, via some element of `RepresentsRelSubPic`, the functor of rigidified line bundles on $X$ rigidified along $\varepsilon$ satisfying the fibrewise condition `algEquivZeroCut`; $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ is assumed smooth and separated. Further data: a representability datum `hreps` for the base change to $k$, an isomorphism `hPk` identifying its Poincaré bundle with the base change to $k$ of the Poincaré bundle of $D$ pulled back along $\mathrm{pr}_1 : D.P \times_A k \to D.P$; designations $D_1, D_2$ for $c_1, c_2$ over $k$ with representability data; and a morphism $\nu_2 : D_k \to D_2$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$ such that for every $k$-scheme $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ and every $T$-point $a$ of $D_k$, the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of $D_2$ along $a$ followed by $\nu_2$ is isomorphic to the rigidification along `rigSection c₂ t ε₂` of the restriction of the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of $D_k$ along $a$ to $C_2 \times_k T$ (`hν₂`).
--
--   *Geometric generic fibre.* Let $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} = \mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\,\mathbb{Q}$ carry $A$- and $L$-algebra structures forming a tower. Let $M_\eta$ be a curve model over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182) (a proper, smooth, integral curve with a prescribed identification of its function field and a bijection `pointEquivPlace` between its $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points and the places of that field), and let $e_\eta : M_\eta.C \to X_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}$ be an isomorphism over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. The hypothesis `hMηpin` pins this identification: for every element $a$ of the finite chart algebra [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L135), the function-field element obtained from $a$ by transport along $e_\eta$ followed by the first projection has Laurent expansion the coefficient image of $a$; the preimage of the finite chart is nonempty. The hypothesis `hgal` states that for every $g \in \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ fixing the image of $L$ pointwise and all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, x'$ of $M_\eta.C$, if $x'$ and $g$-twisted $x$ agree as points of $X$ then `pointEquivPlace` of $x'$ is the translate of `pointEquivPlace` of $x$ by [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54) of $g$.
--
--   *Néron special fibre group data.* Let $G$ be a [`ModularCurve.JOneP.NeronSpecialFibreGeom p`](def/ModularCurve_JOnePGeom.html#L9), consisting of abelian groups $J_{0s}$, $J_I$, $J_E$, a subgroup `torus` of $J_{0s}$ and a surjection $\mathrm{proj} : J_{0s} \to J_I \times J_E$ with kernel `torus`, together with bijections `pts`, `ptsI`, `ptsE` of $J_{0s}$, $J_I$, $J_E$ with the $k$-points of $D_k$, $D_1$, $D_2$ respectively. The hypotheses `hadd`, `haddI`, `haddE` assert additivity of these bijections, in the form that the pullback of the relevant Poincaré bundle along the point attached to a sum is isomorphic to the tensor product of the pullbacks along the summands; `hproj` asserts that for $x \in J_{0s}$ the point attached to the first component of $\mathrm{proj}\,x$ is `pts x` followed by the classifying morphism `RepresentsRelSubPic.pullbackHom` associated with $i_1$, and the point attached to the second component is `pts x` followed by $\nu_2$.
--
--   *Igusa models.* Let $w$ be an integral weight one form over $k$ of level $M$, and let $\mathrm{Mdl}_1, \mathrm{Mdl}_2$ be curve models over $k$ of [`ModularCurve.igusaFunctionFieldX1C k M w`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L35) with isomorphisms $e_1 : \mathrm{Mdl}_1.C \cong C_1$, $e_2 : \mathrm{Mdl}_2.C \cong C_2$ compatible with the structure morphisms.
--
--   *Generic dictionary and Abel–Jacobi map.* Let `gpts` be a bijection from [`ModularCurve.JOne (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L186), the degree-zero divisor class group of `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, to the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of $D$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, additive for the relative group law on $D$ coming from the representability datum (`hgadd`). Let `hDL` be a representability datum for the base change of $X$ to $L$, and $\mathrm{aj}_L : X_L \to D_L$ a morphism over $X_L$'s base such that $\varepsilon_L$ followed by $\mathrm{aj}_L$ is the zero section of $D_L$ (`hajLε`), and such that for every field $K'$, every $t : \operatorname{Spec} K' \to \operatorname{Spec} L$ and every $K'$-point $x$ of $X_L$, the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of $D_L$ along $x$ followed by $\mathrm{aj}_L$ is isomorphic to the tensor product of the line bundle (inverse ideal module) of the relative effective Cartier divisor cut out by $x$ with the ideal module of the divisor cut out by $t$ followed by $\varepsilon_L$ (`hajL`). Let $k_L : X_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}} \to X_L$ be the comparison morphism, characterised by `hkL₁`, `hkL₂` on the two projections, and let $\overline{\mathrm{aj}} : M_\eta.C \to D.P$ be the composite of $e_\eta$, $k_L$, $\mathrm{aj}_L$ and $\mathrm{pr}_1 : D_L \to D.P$, which lies over $M_\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$ followed by $\operatorname{Spec} \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \operatorname{Spec} A$. An isomorphism `hPL` identifies the Poincaré bundle of `hDL` with the base change to $L$ of that of $D$. Let $\overline{\varepsilon}$ be a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of $M_\eta.C$ inducing $\varepsilon$ on $X$ (`hεbar`) and sent by $\overline{\mathrm{aj}}$ to the zero section (`hεbar_aj`). The hypothesis `hpts_aj` states that for all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, s$ of $M_\eta.C$ with $s$ inducing $\varepsilon$, there is a degree-zero divisor $Dv$ on `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` equal to $\mathrm{single}(\mathrm{place}(x),1) - \mathrm{single}(\mathrm{place}(s),1)$ whose class under `gpts` has underlying morphism $x$ followed by $\overline{\mathrm{aj}}$.
--
--   *The place above $p$, the two points, and the hypothesis to be exploited.* Let $Pl$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ in its nonunits (`Pl.LiesOverPrime p`), $\rho : A \to Pl$ a ring homomorphism whose composite with the inclusion $Pl \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the structure map $A \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and $\pi_k : Pl \to k$ a surjection whose composite with $\rho$ is the structure map $A \to k$. Let $P, P'$ be $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of $M_\eta.C$, and let $j_\eta : X_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}} \to X_{Pl}$ be the comparison morphism determined by `hjη₁`, `hjη₂` on the two projections. Let $Dv$ be a degree-zero divisor on `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` with
--   $$Dv = \mathrm{single}(\mathrm{place}(P'),1) - \mathrm{single}(\mathrm{place}(P),1),$$
--   the places being those attached to $P'$ and $P$ by `Mη.pointEquivPlace`. Finally let $a$ be a $Pl$-point of $D$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ through $\rho$, i.e. a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} Pl \to D.P$ whose composite with $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\rho$, and assume (`hz`) that the pullback along $j_\eta$ of the Poincaré bundle of $D$ pulled back along $a$ is isomorphic to
--   $$\mathcal{O}(P') \otimes \mathcal{I}(P),$$
--   that is, the tensor product of the line bundle of the relative effective Cartier divisor on $X_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}$ cut out by $P'$ (viewed in $X$ through $e_\eta$ and the first projection) with the ideal module of the divisor cut out by $P$ in the same way.
--
--   *Conclusion.* The underlying morphism $\operatorname{Spec} \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to D.P$ of the point `gpts (Pic0.mk Dv)` attached to the class of $Dv$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusion $Pl \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ followed by the underlying morphism of $a$.
--
--   This is the generic-fibre half of the Abel–Jacobi dictionary for $X_1(Mp)$: a point of the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ with values in a valuation subring $Pl$ above $p$, whose Poincaré pullback is $\mathcal{O}(P')\otimes\mathcal{O}(P)^{-1}$ on the geometric generic fibre, restricts over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to the point attached by `gpts` to the class $[P']-[P]$. It feeds the two subsequent results which, from such a Poincaré-bundle identification, produce points of $X_1(Mp)$ over valuation subrings together with the corresponding statements about classes in the special fibre of the Néron model.
